A METHOD NOTE THAT COST NOTHING AND WOULD HAVE BEEN BELIEVED. The obvious availability test is
document.fonts.check('16px "Segoe UI"'). In this container it returns TRUE for every family tried,
including families fc-list does not carry at all - Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Ubuntu, Cantarell.
It cannot answer "is this font present". Only the width of a fixed string can. And note the subtler
trap, which is why the sentinel in lib.js is documented narrowly: "Segoe UI" IS absent here and still
does not fall through to the default, because fontconfig SUBSTITUTES Inter - so a font can be missing
and still produce a confident, stable number that is simply wrong against the pins.

WHY THE FULL SUITE WAS NOT RUN, stated plainly because the push bar is normally GATES GREEN.
  1. It CANNOT emit GATES GREEN in this container on ANY tree. Proved on origin/main's OWN bundle
     re-gated unchanged: #479's 58-section run went RED with eleven sections failing, ten of them
     container pins. A subset run cannot emit it by design either. So "the suite is green" is not a
     property this container can establish for an empty change, let alone for mine.
  2. It therefore has ZERO discriminating power about THIS patch. A red suite here is the expected
     reading whether or not my change exists, so it could not distinguish the two.
  3. The before/after control above is a STRICTLY BETTER instrument for the only question that
